<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9261" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοπαῖα</span></b> , only in <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			1.320
		</span></i>
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρνις δ᾽ ὣς ἀνοπαῖα διέπτατο,</span>
		where it is variously written and explained: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> acc. to Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.133
			</span></i>, it is an Adv. (compd. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνά, Ὄπτομαι</span>), she flew away <i>unseen,
				unnoticed;</i> or, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
			</span></i>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνω, ἀνωφερές</span>
			, <i>up into the air,</i> cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρπαλίμως ἀνόπαιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					51
				</span></i>
			, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀνόπαια,</span> the name of
			the pass above Thermopylae (<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.216
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνόπαια</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανόπαια,</span> a kind of <i>eagle,</i> cf.
			Hebr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ̆νᾱπηᾱ</span> 'heron'.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> acc. to Gramm. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				1.83
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀν᾽ ὀπαῖα </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">῀ ῀ἀνὰ ὀπήν</span>) <i>up by the hoie in the
				roof, up the smoke-vent.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>